title: EMR Connect › Sync › What other screens use from EMR Connect
route: /emr
intro: Two other screens lean on EMR Connect. New case can pull a chart only from a Connected system at a site in view, and leaves a field blank while its mapping waits. The Dashboard offers the approval write-back box only while a Connected system at a site in view has its write-back switch on.
dir: TD
also: Found by reading the code and testing the built demo. Disconnect every system and the pull in New case says no records system is connected. Switch write-back off on every row and the Dashboard shows 'Write-back is off for your records system.'
---
screen p1 "EMR Connect\nConnection health, sync, mappings (in Advanced) and the Write back switch on each row"

group gPull "New case: pull a chart"
  click a1 "Click 'Pull a chart from EMR Connect'\nClinical documentation step"
  decision a0 "Is any system at a site in view Connected?"
  toast a8 "'No records system is connected. Connect one in EMR Connect to pull a chart, or drop the files above.'\nWith a link to EMR Connect"
  overlay a2 "Chart from EMR Connect\nDropdown with the charts that live in a Connected system\nA hint under each names the system"
  process a2b "Clinical record · Site A: J.M., 34 · Summit · Residential 3.5 and L.G., 29 · Cardinal · Residential 3.5\nClinical record · Site B: A.R., 45 · Beacon · IOP and S.T., 38 · Harborview · PHP\nA viewer who sees one site is offered only that site's two charts\nA system that is Disconnected or Needs attention offers none"
  input a3 "Pick a chart"
  decision a9 "Does that system still have a field waiting for a mapping?\n'Level of care' or 'Referral source'"
  process a10 "Line under the picker\n'Level of care still needs a mapping there, so that field is left blank.' with 'Open EMR Connect'"
  click a4 "Click 'Pull'\nOr 'Cancel'"
  process a5 "Button reads 'Pulling' for one second"
  store a6 "Case draft is filled in\nPatient, payer, member ID, level of care, request type, diagnoses, reason\nA field that waits for a mapping stays blank"
  toast a7 "'Pulled J.M., 34 from EMR Connect'\n'Everything below was filled in from the chart. You can still change it.'\nOr, amber: 'Level of care needs a mapping, so that field was left blank. You can still fill it in.'"
endgroup
process n1 "Sync now does not add charts to the picker\nThe four charts are fixed. Connect, Disconnect, Fix and Reconnect decide which systems offer them, and Map decides which fields a pull leaves blank"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › New case › Intake › Patient, insurance and request rows"

group gWrite "Dashboard: write back"
  screen b1 "Dashboard request: 'Approved. Write-back waits for you'"
  decision b0 "Does at least one Connected system at a site in view have its write-back switch on?"
  toast b8 "'Write-back is off for your records system.' with 'Turn it on in EMR Connect.'\nInstead of the box. The link opens this page"
  click b2 "Click 'Approve write-back'"
  overlay b3 "Approve the write-back\n'EMR Connect will write only these three things to the chart. No notes, diagnoses or identifiers are written.'"
  process b4 "Approval number, approved amount and dates are listed"
  click b5 "Click 'Write to the EMR'\nOr 'Cancel'"
  ext b6 "The record system receives the three values\nDemo: simulated, about one second"
  store b7 "Request gets 'You confirmed the write-back' and a Cadence event\nToast: 'Written to the EMR'"
endgroup
process n2 "The switch on a Disconnected or Needs attention system does not count\nReconnect it, and the box comes back if its switch is on"
goto g2 "Continues in: Dashboard › Request drawer › Approve the write-back"

p1 -.-> a1
a1 --> a0
a0 -->|No| a8
a0 -->|Yes| a2 --> a2b --> a3 --> a9
a9 -->|Yes| a10 --> a4
a9 -->|No| a4
a4 --> a5 --> a6 --> a7 --> g1
a2 -.-> n1
p1 -.-> b1
b1 --> b0
b0 -->|No| b8
b0 -->|Yes| b2 --> b3 --> b4 --> b5 --> b6 --> b7 --> g2
b8 -.-> n2
